@* ============================================================
   Block: about-founder-letter
   Title: AboutFounderLetter
   Description: A founder letter block for React and Next.js with editorial letter format, four thoughtful paragraphs, italic pull-quote, signature block with name and title, date header, and fade-in entrance animation built with shadcn/ui and Tailwind CSS
   Source: original/blocks/about/about-founder-letter.tsx
   ============================================================ *@

<section class="mx-auto w-full max-w-2xl p-4">
    <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-lg border bg-card">

        @* Header *@
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b px-5 py-4">
            <div>
                <h2 class="text-sm font-medium">A letter from our founder</h2>
                <p class="mt-0.5 text-xs text-muted-foreground">@_signature.Date</p>
            </div>
            <BadgeCn Variant="BadgeVariant.Secondary" Class="text-[10px] font-normal">
                Est. 2020
            </BadgeCn>
        </div>

        @* Letter body *@
        <div class="space-y-5 px-5 py-5">
            @foreach (var paragraph in _paragraphs)
            {
                <p class="text-sm leading-7 text-muted-foreground">@paragraph.Text</p>
            }
        </div>

        @* Pull-quote *@
        <div class="mx-5 mb-5">
            <blockquote class="border-l-2 border-foreground/20 pl-4">
                <p class="text-sm italic leading-6 text-foreground/70">@_pullQuote</p>
            </blockquote>
        </div>

        @* Signature *@
        <div class="border-t px-5 py-4">
            <p class="text-sm font-medium">@_signature.Name</p>
            <p class="mt-0.5 text-xs text-muted-foreground">@_signature.Title</p>
        </div>

    </div>
</section>

@code {
    private record Paragraph(string Id, string Text);

    private record SignatureInfo(string Name, string Title, string Date);

    private static readonly Paragraph[] _paragraphs =
    [
        new("p1", "I spent eight years building developer tools at companies where the tools themselves created more problems than they solved. Every platform promised to simplify workflows, but each one added another dashboard to check, another config file to maintain, another abstraction to learn. The cognitive overhead was crushing. I watched talented engineers spend more time fighting their tools than building products."),
        new("p2", "That frustration became the seed of this company. In early 2020, I started prototyping a system that would do one thing well: get out of the way. No clever abstractions that leak under pressure. No opinionated frameworks that work great for the demo but break under real-world constraints. Just a reliable foundation that lets engineers focus on the problems that actually matter to their users."),
        new("p3", "Six years later, I am still guided by the same principle. We have grown from a weekend project to a team of 48 people serving thousands of engineering teams, and every decision still passes through the same filter: does this reduce complexity, or does it just move complexity somewhere else? If we cannot honestly say it makes an engineer's day simpler, we do not ship it. That means we say no to most feature requests. It means we sometimes take months to get a single interaction right. It means we will never be the tool with the longest feature list, and that is a trade-off I am comfortable with."),
        new("p4", "Thank you for trusting us with your workflows. Whether you joined this week or have been with us since the first beta, your feedback shapes everything we build. I read every support conversation, every feature request, every frustrated tweet. This company exists because engineers like you deserve better tools, and I intend to keep earning that trust one thoughtful release at a time."),
    ];

    private static readonly string _pullQuote =
        "Does this reduce complexity, or does it just move complexity somewhere else? If we cannot honestly say it makes an engineer's day simpler, we do not ship it.";

    private static readonly SignatureInfo _signature = new("Sarah Chen", "Founder & CEO", "March 2026");
}
